TASK-186.1 runtime harness: dev mode's sidebar row (hazard border and host
line) on a normal tab, a pinned tab, a favourite and a split pane, against
non-local rows, light and dark, and following navigation. Temporary code,
never committed to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task186-1-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # fixture pages app/pinned/fav/split.html in $SITE, each a <title> + <h1>:
    python3 -m http.server 8186 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory "$SITE" &
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify1861 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT=8186 \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # a watcher polls $OUT/verify.log every 0.2 s and runs
    # `screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber> $OUT/<name>.png` for each
    # "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>" line (each shot has 2 s before the next
    # change); wait for "done" (about 37 s), then kill that pid and the server.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task186-1-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    rm -r -- ~/Library/Application\ Support/DetourVerify1861

Seeds Dev App (localhost:8186), Remote Docs (a data: page), a pinned tab on
127.0.0.1:8186, favourites on localhost:8186 and on a data: page, and a split
of localhost:8186 (left) with a data: page (right). Each SHOOT also logs every
visible row's title, host line, border frames and label frames, and every
tile's border.

Results (2026-10-24, all eight captures read and matching the log):
- Light and dark, the selected dev row and unselected: Dev App and the pinned
  row show the yellow/black dashed border round the row (x=-6 w=200 h=34, the
  hover rect) and a second line, "localhost:8186" / "127.0.0.1:8186"; the
  cell stays 36 pt (title 16..32, host line 5..18). The split row borders the
  local left half only (w=96), with no host line. The local favourite tile has
  the border, the data: one none. Remote Docs and the Reference pane: nothing.
- Dev App loading a data: page dropped the border and host line ("Left
  Local"); webView.goBack() to localhost restored both.
- The pinned tab loading a data: page dropped them ("Pinned Elsewhere");
  making the entry dormant restored them from the pinned URL (moon badge,
  border, 127.0.0.1:8186).
Not driven: hover over a dev row, a sleeping (not dormant) normal tab, a live
favourite navigating away (covered by DevModeTests).

